# Project_Docs authoring

**Applies when:** Writing or revising design docs agents implement from.

## Embedded markers

- `<<Question: …>>` — ask the agent for clarification on next read.
- `<<Comment: …>>` — area needing author/agent resolution.

## Tiers (see [PROJECT_DOC_INDEX.md](../../Project_Docs/PROJECT_DOC_INDEX.md))

- **Draft_Features/** — work in progress; questions/comments expected.
- **Definitive_Features/** — minimize drift vs code / `project.godot`.
- **Completed_Features/** — snapshots; not default authority unless explicitly cited.

When moving or adding docs, update **only** `PROJECT_DOC_INDEX.md` for path registry changes.

## Splitting large drafts

Before splitting, check whether the feature decomposes into independent subsystems: parts that touch each other only through a one-line interface contract (not shared internals), could be implemented/tested without the rest of the doc open, and could plausibly promote to `Definitive_Features/` on a different schedule. If so, prefer several `<FEATURE>_<SUBSYSTEM>_RESOLVED.md` contracts over one `<FEATURE>_RESOLVED.md` — apply this same size gate recursively to each. `<FEATURE>_IMPLEMENTATION.md` stays a **single feature-level file** regardless — build order/gating spans subsystems and doesn't decompose the same way a contract does.

A `Draft_Features/<FEATURE>.md` that crosses **~20,000 characters (~5,000 tokens)** should split into three files so implementation work doesn't require loading rationale/history to find "what's next":

- **`<FEATURE>_RESOLVED.md`** — current contract only: formulas, schemas, config keys, one-line "why" per non-obvious call. No narrative. `<<Question>>`/`<<Comment>>` markers still apply here. Promotes to `Definitive_Features/` once implementation + testing land.
- **`<FEATURE>_HISTORY.md`** — full decision narrative: superseded approaches, discovery notes, why we got here. Not a routine agent read — pull in only when asked "why did we do X." Promotes to `Completed_Features/` alongside `_RESOLVED.md`'s promotion.
- **`<FEATURE>_IMPLEMENTATION.md`** — phase/status tracking, what's next. Deleted once the feature ships to `main`.

Trigger on first crossing the size gate, going forward — don't split an existing large doc unless asked.

## Code ↔ doc sync playbook

**Applies when:** Syncing active Project_Docs after a code or config change (see [core.mdc](./core.mdc) **Doc sync**).

### Find the doc

| Signal | Action |
|--------|--------|
| `## …` link in changed `.gd` / `.tscn` header | Primary target + section |
| Task cites `Draft_Features/FOO.md` | That file is authoritative for the task |
| Index “Notes” column names a canonical doc for the topic | Use that path |
| Definitive “usage map” exists for the subsystem | Update map tables / snapshot paragraph |

### What to update (minimum useful sync)

- Renamed/moved scripts → path tables and cross-links in the doc
- New/changed `@export`, `pack_resources.json` keys, `project.godot` layers → definitive tables (e.g. [ENVIRONMENT_MODEL_PLAN.md §6](../../Project_Docs/Definitive_Features/ENVIRONMENT_MODEL_PLAN.md))
- New consumer of a trait/stat/config → row in usage-map docs ([CREATURE_TRAIT_USAGE.md](../../Project_Docs/Definitive_Features/CREATURE_TRAIT_USAGE.md), [CREATURE_ATTRIBUTES_USAGE.md](../../Project_Docs/Definitive_Features/CREATURE_ATTRIBUTES_USAGE.md))
- Shipped acceptance criterion → check box in draft §6 or definitive checklist
- Behavior change under active refactor → [CREATURE_MOVEMENT_V2.md](../../Project_Docs/Draft_Features/CREATURE_MOVEMENT_V2.md) (design) **and** [CREATURE_MOVEMENT.md](../../Project_Docs/Definitive_Features/CREATURE_MOVEMENT.md) (inventory) when the inventory is affected

### What not to do

- Don’t paste large code blocks — keep path + contract summaries (match existing definitive style)
- Don’t update `Completed_Features/` to reflect new behavior
- Don’t create duplicate topics — one canonical path per index row

### Promotion

When a draft feature becomes an ongoing contract, promote per index **Promotion** table in the same change set as the shipping code (move file, index row, delete draft copy, fix links).

### Verification before finishing

Grep changed symbols/paths against `Project_Docs/` for stale references; confirm linked section still describes behavior.
